# School Reform in the Russian Republic: An Interview with Edward Dneprov.

**Authors:** Rust, Val D.

## Abstract
According to Education Minister Edward Dneprov, the Russian Republic's education policy has two major pillars--democratization and &quot;humanitization&quot; (stressing the humanities and a truly child-centered curriculum). A market economy is not incompatible with humanistic aims, but it is not the driving force behind them. The flagging economy is the major stumbling block to education reform. (MLH)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ437607

